{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>As I go out of the city.</b> Since it said above 'whoever is found in the field' and the hail came down upon them, now at the time of the plague, lest they say he is afraid to go out because of the hail, he said: as I go out of the city, I will spread my hands, and I am not afraid of the hail. Another interpretation: <b>as I go out</b> from you, to come into the city — I will spread my hands inside the city. And so it says: 'And Moses went out from Pharaoh, et ha'ir' etc. Another interpretation, according to the plain sense: the plague of hail strikes in the field more than in the city; therefore he said: as I go out of the city, I will see the devastation of the hail in the field, and I will pray as needed." "<b>[As I go out of the city.</b> From the city.]"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:46.882150056Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}